            <div xml:id="d309">

                <pb facs="0254" n="242" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg242"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710.Consultation(2)/414: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the American Delegate</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Hull</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-07-24T20:00:00-04:00">July 24, 1940—8 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>25. For White from the Secretary of the Treasury. Reference your 9, July 23, 6
                    p.m. I am willing to go along provided the Government and Central Bank of each
                    particular country would guarantee individually and collectively the gold loan.
                    [Morgenthau.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
